The supplied semantics directly supports the canonical solution: convert the integer once, reverse with a `-1` slice when the shift exceeds the digit count, otherwise concatenate the two complementary slices. I’m using that form because it preserves the prompt’s edge behavior (including shift zero) and maps entirely to existing `str`, `len`, comparison, and slicing rules.
apply patch
