codex
The first proof attempt exposed a prover limitation rather than a program counterexample: the backend did not use `SHIFT <= length` to reduce the already-computed Boolean `SHIFT > length` when that length is the symbolic digit-string length. I’m adding a narrowly scoped verification lemma for the `If` continuation that expresses integer trichotomy; it does not alter the supplied semantics or the program.
apply patch
